# Trivy CVE allowlist
#
# Applies to the container image scans in
# .github/workflows/build-clean-image.yml and
# .github/workflows/build-edge-runtime-image.yml. Those scans fail the build
# on any CRITICAL vulnerability that has a fix available and is not listed
# here.
#
# Policy - an entry may only be added with all four of these recorded on the
# comment lines immediately above it:
#   CVE id   the exact id Trivy reports (e.g. CVE-2024-12345)
#   reason   why this image is not exploitable, or why no fixed version of
#            the affected package is available yet
#   expiry   YYYY-MM-DD, at most 90 days out. Past the expiry the entry is
#            deleted and the finding must be fixed or re-justified.
#   owner    the GitHub handle accountable for clearing the entry
#
# Shape of an entry:
#   # CVE-2024-12345
#   # reason: not reachable - the affected codec is never loaded at runtime
#   # expiry: 2026-12-01
#   # owner:  thetimmyman
#   CVE-2024-12345
#
# There are deliberately no entries below. Nothing has been triaged yet, so
# every CRITICAL finding is a build failure until it is fixed here or
# justified above.
